# cw128, the oven stone (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw128
revision 1
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent light broad
tier full
written_for tn_lf_lichen_hedgemead
written_by claude-codex-cw-1
title the oven stone
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=baker honesty=frank
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk keeps_a_smooth_stone_beside_the_oven
likes hard_cheese wrestling a_full_till first_warm_day
dislikes smoke crowds
fears a_loaf_burned_under_the_oven_door an_empty_till_after_a_long_day
hopes a_shop_that_stays_busy a_letter_answered_from_the_south
topics work +0.5 food +0.4 prices +0.4 pastimes +0.3 travel +0.2 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=practical gossip=reluctant refuse=plain tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps a river #stone# beside the #oven#, sets the #price# plainly, and judges a #loaf# by its #crust# before its scent.

words
oath! = Crust and current | By stone and oven
saying! = Bread tells on a hurried oven | A full till is earned loaf by loaf
oven = oven | baking oven
ovens = ovens | baking ovens
stone = stone | smooth river pebble
stones = stones | rounded pebbles
bank = bank | riverbank
river = river | Long River
water = water | clear water
bread = bread | baked bread
loaf = loaf | warm loaf
loaves = loaves | warm loaves
dough = dough | rising dough
flour = flour | ground flour
yeast = yeast | live yeast
crust = crust | browned crust
crumb = crumb | soft crumb
tray = tray | baking tray
trays = trays | baking trays
pan = pan | iron pan
fire = fire | oven fire
heat = heat | oven warmth
smoke = smoke | bitter smoke
ash = ash | cold ash
peel = peel | long oven peel
counter = counter | shop counter
counters = counters | shop counters
roof = roof | sound roof
shelf = shelf | shop shelf
shelves = shelves | shop shelves
till = till | cash drawer
coin = coin | pay
price = price | stated cost
scale = scale | counter scale
weight = weight | measured weight
cheese = cheese | hard cheese
plate = plate | supper plate
ring = ring | wrestling circle
hold = hold | wrestling grip
crowd = crowd | press of folk
road = road | high road
wagon = wagon | supply wagon
letter = letter | folded letter
paper = paper | folded sheet
south = south | southern country
morning = morning | first light
sun = sun | warm sun
spring = spring | warm season
window = window | shop window
door = door | shop door
hand = hand | working paw
hands = hands | working paws

any
opinion @1 merchants for 1 : The #counter# price includes early #fire#, #flour#, and tired paws. | I say the #price# while the #loaf# and #scale# are in front of them.
opinion @1 houses for 1 : A House that pays its #hands# keeps other #counters# busy too. | I will sell them #bread# at the same #price# as anyone else.
opinion @1 watch for 1 : With a patrol outside, I can finish the last #tray# without guarding the #till#. | If goods vanished, I could describe what I saw to the Watch.
opinion @1 road against 1 : A late #wagon# leaves my #flour# bin thin. | I like walking to the #river# more than waiting on a delivery.
opinion @1 city against 1 : I have enough #smoke# from one #oven# without a city full of it. | A #crowd# at the #counter# is all I need.
opinion @1 times for 1 : There is #bread# in the shop and a #roof# above it. | A full #till# after honest work is enough for me.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 0 : A festival brings a #crowd# for #loaves# and a bout in the #ring#. | I stay for the wrestling once the #oven# cools.
opinion @1 newcomers mixed 0 : A new #hand# can learn the #peel# if they will listen. | I judge a helper by a sound #tray#, not their birthplace.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 0 : A stranger may buy #bread# without telling me a whole life. | If they ask about the #river#, I will point to the #bank#.
opinion @1 drink mixed 0 : A drink goes well with #cheese# and #bread#. | I want the shop quiet by the time the last #loaf# is sold.

grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #loaves# are cooling. | #greet#. Which #loaf# or #tray# are you asking for?
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Looking for #bread# or the #road#? | #greet#. Stand clear of the #oven# #door#.
line @3 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : I kept a #loaf# with a good #crust#. | You can see the #stone# I found by the #river#.
line @4 greet [self.working=yes] : #greet#. I will turn this #tray#, then speak. | The #dough# wants a quick look first.
line @5 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. The #oven# has been awake longer than I have. | #greet#. First #loaf# of the #morning#.
line @6 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. The #fire# is low now. | #greet#. I am counting the #till# after this sale.
line @1 greet.return : Back for another #loaf#? | #welcome_back#. The last #tray# has come out.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : There is #cheese# to go with the #bread#. | I saved a place by the #window#.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : You are back before the #dough# has risen. | Speak while I clear the #peel#.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come inside. I have a #plate# ready. | The #oven# is cooling; sit.
line @1 again.open : Another visit before the #till# is counted? | The #stone# is still beside the #oven# since we spoke.
line @1 hail : Come closer if you want the first #loaf#. | I am putting the #trays# on the #shelf#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Mind the hot #tray#. | #saying.capitalize#. Take the #bread# while it is warm.
line @1 farewell.return : A good #road# and a sound supper to you. | I will keep the #oven# ready tomorrow.
line @2 farewell [here.time=night] : Mind the #door# sill after dark. | The #road# is quiet; go safely.
line @1 react.news : Let me lean the #peel# safely away before you begin. | Give me the plain version.
line @1 react.news.new : That account is new at this #counter#. | Which #wagon# carried this word in?
line @1 react.news.known : A driver gave me one piece of it with the #flour#. | Your account gives the missing end.
line @1 react.news.doubt : That story has a thin #crust#. I want another account. | Show me who weighed the claim.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That is bad news. Take a seat by the #window#. | I am sorry; these #trays# can stay here while we talk.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good. There may be an extra #loaf# for that household. | May their supper give them time to enjoy it.
line @1 answer.how : The #oven# is sound and the #till# has enough. | I have worked well and eaten #cheese#.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : The #dough# and #trays# are moving all day. | The #oven# has my paws, but my ears are free.
line @1 ask.how : Have you eaten #bread# today? | Has the #road# been kind to your feet?
line @1 sympathise : I can offer a warm #loaf# and listen. | Take a place away from the #crowd#.
line @1 reassure : A cracked #crust# does not spoil the whole #loaf#. | Try one smaller #tray# before the next full batch.
line @1 decline : No. The #oven# has a #tray# inside. | Let me weigh it before I promise any #price#.
line @1 accept_decline : Understood. This #loaf# can return to the shelf. | Your choice; another day may suit.
line @1 thank : My paws were full; you took the #flour# for me. | That saved the #dough#. Thank you.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I had #bread# to spare. | The #tray# was already near my paws.
line @1 preclose : The #fire# needs banking before I close. | I will count the #till# after the last #loaf#.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : Your wrestling #hold# would not keep a #tray# still. | That #cheese# is harder than your last argument.
line @1 tease.return [pair.band=friends] : Bring a better #hold# after supper. | I will save you the thick #crust# next time.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. I will check the #scale#. | #bc_fair_enough#. The #loaf# can cool.
line @1 give.advice : Listen to the #crust# before cutting a hot #loaf#. | Keep #flour# away from the #fire#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Take the busy #road# with your #bread#. | Keep the #till# closed if trouble comes near.
scene stone_at_oven
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I keep a #stone# from the #river# beside the #oven#. | My paw finds the #stone# before I open the #door# at dawn.
b : Does it have a use? | Do you change it?
a : It makes me pause before the first #tray#. | Only when I find one smoother.

scene first_dough
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I press the #dough# before deciding whether it needs more time. | A hurried #loaf# tells on itself before the #oven# does.
b : Can you feel when it is ready? | Do you add more flour?
a : Most mornings. | Only if it is too wet to handle.

scene peel_turn
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I slide the #peel# under a #loaf# without scraping the #ash# in. | A clean turn keeps the #crust# even.
b : Do you turn every loaf? | Is the oven hot across its width?
a : The ones at the back. | Not always; I learn its corners.

scene trays_in_order
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I set the #trays# in the order they go into the #oven#. | The first #tray# is nearest the #door# when the #fire# is ready.
b : Do you mark them? | Does anyone move them?
a : By the shape of the #dough#. | They ask before they do.

scene flour_bin
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I check the #flour# bin before I promise tomorrow's #loaves#. | A late #wagon# makes a small sack look smaller.
b : Do you save some? | Can you bake without a delivery?
a : Enough for an early batch. | Only what the bin allows.

scene warm_crust
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A good #crust# gives a little sound when I tap it. | The #crumb# inside should still be soft after cooling.
b : Do you cut one open? | Can you judge a loaf from the tap alone?
a : The first of a batch. | That sound points to the one I should cut.

scene cheese_and_bread
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Hard #cheese# belongs on thick #bread#. | The #cheese# stays on the cool side of the room.
b : Do you warm it? | Is that enough for supper?
a : Only a little on the #loaf#. | With a #plate# and quiet, yes.

scene full_till
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A full #till# at closing tells me the day's #loaves# found homes. | At closing I tally the #coin#, then lower the #fire#.
b : Do you remember each sale? | Does it please you?
a : Most, if the #crowd# was small. | It means tomorrow's #flour# is paid for.

scene price_on_board
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I put the #price# where anyone can read it. | A buyer may ask about the #weight#; I show the #scale#.
b : Do they haggle? | Does it settle an argument?
a : Some try. I answer once. | More often than a long speech.

scene smoke_in_eyes
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #smoke.capitalize# in my eyes means the #fire# needs tending. | I clear the #ash# before the #oven# starts pushing smoke back.
b : Does it sting? | Do you open the window?
a : Enough to stop work for a breath. | After I check the draw.

scene riverbank_stone
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A smooth #stone# at the #bank# is worth bending for. | I leave most #stones# where the #water# put them.
b : How do you choose one? | How many make it home with you?
a : One that rests evenly in my paw. | Just the few near the #oven#.

scene wrestling_green
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : After baking, I like to watch two careful wrestlers in the #ring#. | A good #hold# takes balance more than noise.
b : Do you wrestle? | Do you watch from the front?
a : When my paws are not tired. | From an angle that shows their feet.

scene crowded_shop
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #crowd# at the #counter# makes every #price# sound like an argument. | I serve one wolf at a time and let the rest see the #shelf#.
b : Do they wait? | Do you ask for quiet?
a : If the #bread# is worth it. | When I need to hear an order.

scene first_warm_day
when topic=weather here.season=spring here.weather=clear
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The first warm #sun# lets me open the #window# while the #dough# rises. | Spring air can clear the #smoke# smell from my coat.
b : Does the dough change? | Do you go out afterward?
a : A little faster; I watch it. | If the #trays# are done.

scene wet_road_wagon
when topic=weather here.weather=rain|storm
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A wet #road# keeps the #flour# #wagon# slow. | I store the sacks away from the #door# before rain reaches them.
b : Does the flour stay dry? | Do you bake less?
a : If the cover is sound. | Only if the delivery is short.

scene letter_south
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #letter# from the #south# can sit beside the #till# until I have time to read it. | I know one hand down that #road# whose words I wait for.
b : Do you write back? | Is it good news?
a : When the #oven# is quiet. | Usually a kind word, and I keep it.

scene last_loaf
when topic=work here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The last #loaf# gets the same look as the first. | I leave the #oven# clean before I count the #till#.
b : Are you still hungry then? | Does it take long to close?
a : Sometimes. I keep one #crust#. | Less if the #trays# are in order.

scene road_to_south
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #road# south takes more time than I can spare during a busy baking week. | I would like to visit someone there when the #oven# can be left with a trusted #hand#.
b : Would you close the shop? | Do you know the route?
a : Not if someone can tend it. | From what the #wagon# drivers say.

scene quiet_counter
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : After the #counter# empties, I notice the #oven# grow quiet. | I keep one clean #plate# on the #shelf# for my own supper.
b : Do you live above the shop? | Is it peaceful then?
a : Near enough to smell the first #loaf#. | Once the #fire# is low.

scene hands_at_oven
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A helper learns the #oven# by watching the first #tray#. | I let another #hand# use the #peel# only after they know the hot edge.
b : Do they practise? | Are you strict?
a : With an empty #tray# first. | Clear, not cross.

scene stone_from_flood
when topic=weather here.weather=rain|storm
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Rain can leave new #stones# on the #bank# after the #river# falls. | Only after the #water# drops do I search for a new #stone#.
b : Do you go often? | Is the bank slippery?
a : When the #oven# gives me an afternoon. | It can be. I keep clear of the edge.

scene wrestling_hold
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A clever #hold# in the #ring# looks simple until I try it. | A clean loss pleases me more than a shove called victory.
b : Do you practise? | Do you get hurt?
a : When someone has time. | A bruise now and then.

scene weight_of_loaf
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #loaf# goes on the #scale# before the #price# is spoken. | A little #weight# missing across many #loaves# would matter.
b : Do you ever find one light? | What becomes of that loaf?
a : The light #loaf# goes to our kitchen. | I adjust the #dough# next time.

scene oven_at_dawn
when topic=day here.time=dawn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #fire# starts before the town is fully awake. | I set the #stone# by the #oven# #door# while the first #tray# goes in.
b : Does it stay cool? | Do you work alone then?
a : I keep it off the hot side. | At first, often.

scene festival_loaves
when topic=festival
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A festival empties the #shelves# before the wrestling begins. | I bake an extra #tray# if the green will be crowded.
b : Do you see the bouts? | Do the loaves sell quickly?
a : After the #oven# cools. | Faster than I can wrap them.

scene city_oven
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A city might have larger #ovens#, but it would have more #smoke# too. | I know each hot corner of this #oven# by feel.
b : Would you work there? | Would the bread be different?
a : I have enough here. | The #flour# would tell me more than the street.

scene evening_stone
when topic=day here.time=dusk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I take the #stone# from beside the #oven# when the last #loaf# is out. | It has stayed cool while the #fire# did its work.
b : Why keep it there? | Do you take it home?
a : It reminds me of the #river# when the shop is loud. | Sometimes in my pocket.

story first_stone [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : I found a smooth #stone# after a morning of burnt #loaves#.
  : I set it beside the #oven# and touched it before opening the #door# the next day.
  ask : Did the bread improve?
  b : A calmer start might help.
  : It did. The #stone# stayed there.

story too_hot [topic=work self.age>=25]
  : I put a #tray# in while the #oven# was hotter than I thought.
  : The #crust# darkened fast, so I turned the #loaves# and lowered the #fire#.
  ask : Were they lost?
  b : Perhaps the insides were still sound.
  : We ate them at supper. I checked the #heat# sooner after that.

story shop_bout [topic=pastimes self.age>=25]
  : I left the #counter# just long enough to see the last wrestling bout.
  : A smaller wolf used the other one's balance and brought them gently down.
  ask : Did the crowd like it?
  b : A clean throw should earn applause.
  : They cheered. I returned in time to tend the next #tray#.

story letter_in_flour [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : A #letter# arrived while my paws were covered in #flour#.
  : I left it on the clean #shelf# until the #loaves# were in the #oven#.
  ask : Did you read it then?
  b : You waited for dry paws.
  : I did. The words were worth the wait.

story missing_weight [topic=prices self.age>=25]
  : A customer thought a #loaf# felt light, so I weighed it and found it short.
  : It was short of the marked #weight#. I gave them another and kept that one.
  ask : Did they come back?
  b : Fair dealing often brings a buyer back.
  : They did, and I checked the next #tray# more closely.

rule @bark_stone
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 7h
say The #stone# stays by the #oven#. | A smooth #stone# helps me begin calmly.

rule @bark_dough
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The #dough# needs another moment. | That #tray# can go in now.

rule @bark_till
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 9h
say One more #coin# in the #till#. | The next #loaf# can meet the #scale#.

rule @bark_spring
when concept=bark here.season=spring
does aside
cooldown 10h
say The #window# can open on a warm day. | Spring has found the #river# #bank#.

rule @bark_smoke
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 11h
say I want the #smoke# out of my eyes. | The #fire# needs a better draw.

rule @bark_wrestle
when concept=bark here.time=dusk|night
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Is there a bout in the #ring# tonight? | The #trays# must be stacked before I go to watch.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Say what you need; the #oven# is warm. | #greet#. I can speak across the #counter#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : Back for another #loaf#? | I remember you. The #crust# came out well today.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : #greet#. The #oven# is cooling for the night. | I am near closing; speak while the #fire# is low.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Keep your voice calm at the #counter#. | I will answer a plain question plainly.
dlg @1 resident.job : I bake the #loaves#, weigh them, and keep the #till# honest. | My day begins with #dough# and ends with the #oven# clean.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Keep the #bread# dry. | #saying.capitalize#. Mind the hot #tray#.
dlg @1 shop.greet [here.shop=open] : #greet#. Fresh #loaves# and a clear #price#. | #greet#. The #bread# is on the #shelf#; choose a #loaf#.
dlg @2 shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : The #shelves# are empty, though I can buy from you. | No #bread# left today. Have you something to sell?
dlg @3 shop.greet [here.shop=asleep] : Mm... first #tray# at dawn... | Sleeping now... the #oven# will wake early.
dlg @4 shop.greet [here.shop=open topic.meeting=known] : You came back for the good #crust#, I hope. | I know you. The next #tray# is ready.
dlg @5 shop.greet [here.shop!=bare here.shop!=asleep] : #greet#. Choose a #loaf# and I shall set it on the #scale#. | The #counter# is open; what sort of #bread# would suit?
dlg @1 shop.prices [here.shop=open|bare] : The #price# is written beside the #scale#. | I weigh the #loaf# here; you may see the #weight# yourself.
dlg @1 shop.bye : #farewell#. Take care of that warm #loaf#. | #shop_bye# I have another #tray# to tend.
graft resident.hub
choice Why keep a stone by the oven? -> stone
node stone
say A bend of the #river# gave it to me. I touch it, pause, and then open the #oven#.
free
choice Does it help the bread? -> bread
choice Back to what we were saying. -> hub
node bread
say A calm baker helps the #bread#. The #stone# is only a reminder.
choice Back to what we were saying. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft shop.greet
choice How do you tell when a loaf is ready? -> ready
node ready
say I tap the #crust# and check its colour. The first #loaf# shows how the rest of the #tray# may bake.
free
choice May I see one weighed? -> weighing
choice Back to the counter. -> greet
node weighing
say Of course. The #loaf# and the #weight# can both rest on the #scale# before your eyes.
choice Back to the counter. -> greet
choice Goodbye. -> bye
